    "id": "BLK_FS_02",
    "type": "history",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "estimated_minutes": 3,
    "bloom": "Understand",
    "content": "Cultural Integration: In ancient India, the concept of 'Annadaan' (the giving of food) was considered the highest form of charity (Maha Daan). The Taittiriya Upanishad famously declares: 'Annam Na Nindyat, Tadvratam' (Do not disrespect food, that is a vow) and 'Annam Bahu Kurvita' (Grow food in abundance). The modern concept of Food Security is rooted in these ancient principles of ensuring no one goes hungry.",
    "body": "Cultural Integration: In ancient India, the concept of 'Annadaan' (the giving of food) was considered the highest form of charity (Maha Daan). The Taittiriya Upanishad famously declares: 'Annam Na Nindyat, Tadvratam' (Do not disrespect food, that is a vow) and 'Annam Bahu Kurvita' (Grow food in abundance). The modern concept of Food Security is rooted in these ancient principles of ensuring no one goes hungry."
  },
